frps for Debian
---------------

The frps service is installed but not enabled or started: with
upstream's example configuration it would accept any client. Set a token
(and anything else you need) in /etc/frp/frps.toml first, e.g.

  bindPort = 7000
  auth.token = "a long random string"

then check it and start the service:

  frps verify -c /etc/frp/frps.toml
  systemctl enable --now frps

frps runs as the frp user, which can bind ports below 1024
(vhostHTTPPort = 80, vhostHTTPSPort = 443). For more than one server,
frps@<name>.service reads /etc/frp/<name>.toml.

The dashboard needs webServer.port (and webServer.user and
webServer.password) in the configuration. frps logs to the journal unless
log.to names a file; files in /var/log/frp are writable for the service.

The full configuration reference is
/usr/share/doc/frps/frps_full_example.toml.
